<settings version="2">
    <!-- The weather provider. ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING across CLASSES, not just
         within this fragment: Kodi validates an addon-type setting against
         its installed, enabled add-ons and rejects an id it does not know, so
         this set only works because the plan enables every class D add-on
         (weather.multi among them) BEFORE any class A set runs (plan 7.4
         steps 3 then 4). weather.multi ships in this bundle's addons/ with
         its four pure-python deps; its remaining deps resolve on every box
         (script.module.pil is bundled inside each platform's Kodi build -
         measured in Kodi.app 22.0b1, and absent from ts1's userdata addons
         after a real install - and script.module.requests is this add-on's
         own hard dependency, so it exists wherever this profile can run).

         Value measured off the owner's hand-set ts1, 2026-08-31. The location
         itself is addon data, not a core id: addon_data/weather.multi/
         settings.xml in this bundle.

         Apple TV note, not a gate: on tvOS Multi Weather only RUNS because
         service.tvos.pythonfix shims the _scproxy module Kodi's tvOS build
         dropped (anything touching urllib dies at import without it). The
         install and this provider set are correct regardless; the fix add-on
         is user-installed per that add-on's own contract. -->
    <setting id="weather.addon">weather.multi</setting>
</settings>
